// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`browser steering for refusals, files, and pending surfaces is the same text for every caller, apart from the search tool name 1`] = `"Preferred workflow: call browser.list, reuse or open a browser, call browser.input_snapshot with role/inputType/fuzzy-name filters, act with the returned refs, then take a new input snapshot after navigation. Elements in iframes have their own refs; frame narrows a locator to one frame. A locator is a CSS selector or one of page.locator(), page.getByTestId(), page.getByRole(), page.getByLabel(), page.getByPlaceholder(), page.getByAltText(), and page.getByText(), optionally inside page.frameLocator(). On every command for an existing tab, pass its profile.runtimeGeneration from browser.open or browser.list as expectedRuntimeGeneration. Paginate with nextOffset when truncated is true. When an action returns a pending JavaScript dialog, including prompt(), use browser.handle_dialog with its dialogId; include promptText when accepting a prompt. browser.get_dialog also reports a pending file chooser, print request, or sign-in: answer a chooser with browser.upload_files and its chooserId, and use browser.handle_dialog to save a print request as a PDF, to dismiss a chooser or a print request, or to cancel a sign-in; only the user can sign in. Use dialogResponse on a click or key press as an optional optimization when the response is known in advance. A handledDialog result confirms the pre-armed dialog response was applied and the action completed. Click, fill, press, set_checked, select_option, type, focus, wait_for, hover, scroll, and drag results include a receipt: check its status (an outcome_unknown action may have happened, so inspect the page before retrying) and read error.details when an action is refused. A not_executed receipt says why in error and what to call next in error.next; a warning that the target was covered means a banner or overlay may need closing. Use browser.select_option to choose options and browser.set_checked to check or uncheck controls; do not use browser.click for either. Use browser.type for masked inputs and autocomplete, and browser.fill for ordinary fields. For autocomplete, wait for suggestions and click one instead of pressing Enter. Read readback before assuming a value took. Use browser.scroll instead of repeated snapshots to reach content below the fold and in virtualized or infinite lists; check effects.scroll.atEnd and contentGrew (atStart for up/left). Scroll effects are point-in-time observations; lazy content may arrive later, so wait or scroll again. Use browser.hover to open hover menus; input_snapshot lists only controls, so target other elements with a CSS locator or x and y. A negative y moves the pointer off the page, which triggers exit-intent popups. Use browser.drag for sortable lists and boards within one document. Use browser.wait_for to wait for an element, text, URL, or load state instead of polling snapshots; its observed.matchCount and visibleCount count the elements a locator matches. Downloads appear in effects.downloads and browser.list_transfers; browser.save_download copies one into the workspace. Uploads need the user’s approval; for a file outside the workspace, call browser.request_files so the user can pick it. Pass an actionId when a browser action may be retried. Avoid probing many generic selectors or parallelizing state-changing browser actions. Screenshots are returned as viewable image content and are best for visual confirmation; input_snapshot is best for discovering controls; to read text such as a result message, browser.inspect its element. Use SearchActions only when the dispatch schema does not provide enough detail."`;
